.TH qsh-trust-rename 1  "rename 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-trust\-rename \- Rename a pinned peer (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11). Takes effect at the next handshake with no restart required. `acl.toml` is not reloaded: until `qsh serve`/`qsh listen` restarts with a row for the new name, the renamed peer matches no row and is denied (default\-deny); rows naming the old principal no longer apply to it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh trust rename\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIOLD\fR> <\fINEW\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rename a pinned peer (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11). Takes effect at the next handshake with no restart required. `acl.toml` is not reloaded: until `qsh serve`/`qsh listen` restarts with a row for the new name, the renamed peer matches no row and is denied (default\-deny); rows naming the old principal no longer apply to it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIOLD\fR>
The peer\*(Aqs current trust\-store name
.TP
<\fINEW\fR>
The name to rename it to
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
